:: c01s01p01
<<set $stress = Math.max(0, Math.min(100, $stress + 6))>>
The attic air is cold and river-damp; Leon sits muttering at the center, hunched in the dark. Your breath fogs, and the rafters listen for what you will do without speaking.
<p class="dialogue">You stood up here too? Thought so. This place keeps the heat it steals. Don't get ideas about warming it.</p>
<p class="dialogue">I don't owe you a show. If you're waiting me out, you'll be here a while. People always blink first.</p>
<p class="dialogue">Boxes, drafts, a roof that leaks when it remembers. That's all. And a man who ran out of exits.</p>
<<timedprogressbar $timer>>
  <<goto "c01s01p02">>
<</timedprogressbar>>
[[Act: Hold the gaze|c01s01p03]]

:: c01s01p02
<<set $stress = Math.max(0, Math.min(100, $stress + 4))>>
Shadows crease along rafters as you linger. The hush tightens; his shoulder twitches like a clock hand refusing to move. Dust pricks your throat with the old wood's breath.
<p class="dialogue">You're still here. Figure the quiet will tell you something? It does. It says mind your distance.</p>
<p class="dialogue">I used to listen to the river from here. Easier than listening to people. The river doesn't ask for anything.</p>
<<timedprogressbar $timer>>
  <<goto "c01s01p03">>
<</timedprogressbar>>
[[Act: Lower your gaze|c01s01p04]]

:: c01s01p03
<<set $stress = Math.max(0, Math.min(100, $stress + 2))>>
His posture repeats yesterday's weight. You steady yourself; the beams above seem to press down until your calves quiver with the held stillness.
<p class="dialogue">Steady as a nail, huh. Try being that steady when the board splits under you. That's life. Split boards.</p>
<p class="dialogue">You think I'm about to turn and confess? I don't turn anymore. I pivot the whole room instead.</p>
<<timedprogressbar $timer>>
  <<goto "c01s01p05">>
<</timedprogressbar>>
[[Act: Glance at the attic|c01s01p05]]

:: c01s01p04
<<set $stress = Math.max(0, Math.min(100, $stress + 3))>>
You tilt your gaze into the darkness. Dust motes rise like doubts, catching the faintest light. Leon faces the wall; the center of the floor feels alarmingly near.
<p class="dialogue">Eyes down is smart. You won't trip over anything you don't name. Keep it that way.</p>
<p class="dialogue">Walls take what you tell them and give it back colder. I've learned to stop telling.</p>
<<timedprogressbar $timer>>
  <<goto "c01s01p06">>
<</timedprogressbar>>
[[Act: Look into the darkness|c01s01p09]]

:: c01s01p05
<<set $stress = Math.max(0, Math.min(100, $stress + 2))>>
You sweep the beams with your eyes. The center listens; patience thickens in your throat, as if waiting could tip the floor one way or the other.
<p class="dialogue">Careful with that patience. It starts like mercy and ends like neglect if you let it.</p>
<p class="dialogue">Don't look for treasure. I packed the good parts in lies and sent them downriver.</p>
<<timedprogressbar $timer>>
  <<goto "c01s01p06">>
<</timedprogressbar>>
[[Act: Notice the notes|c01s01p07]]

:: c01s01p06
<<set $anger = Math.max(0, Math.min(100, $anger + 2))>>
He mutters to himself, barely acknowledging you. The hush is brittle; your muscles argue between holding and moving. A draft threads along your wrist.
<p class="dialogue">Don't touch me. That's the rule you haven't been told yet. Learn it fast.</p>
<p class="dialogue">I can feel you measuring me. Put away your tape. I'm not a project.</p>
<<if visited("c01s01p11") >= 1 || visited("c01s01p14") >= 1>>
  <<timedprogressbar $timer>>
    <<goto "c02s01p01">>
  <</timedprogressbar>>
<<else>>
  <<timedprogressbar $timer>>
    <<goto "c01s01p05">>
  <</timedprogressbar>>
<</if>>
[[Act: Rest a hand on Leon's shoulder|c01s01p16]]
[[Act: Touch Leon's back|c01s01p16]]
[[Act: Brush Leon's arm|c01s01p16]]

:: c01s01p07
<<set $stress = Math.max(0, Math.min(100, $stress + 5))>>
A scrap of paper near him lies creased. The boxy folds whisper I wrote notes here once. You notice the notes, ink bled by humidity, edges soft as old cloth.
<p class="dialogue">Don't read those. They're not prayers and they never helped. Paper soaks up shame and drips it back slow.</p>
<p class="dialogue">If you pick one, pick it like it's a splinter. It'll sting either way.</p>
<<if visited("c01s01p01") >= 1>>
  <<timedprogressbar $timer>>
    <<goto "c01s01p10">>
  <</timedprogressbar>>
<<else>>
  <<timedprogressbar $timer>>
    <<goto "c01s01p08">>
  <</timedprogressbar>>
<</if>>
[[Act: Pick up the notes|c01s01p08]]
[[Act: Point at the notes|c01s01p08]]

:: c01s01p08
<<set $stress = Math.max(0, Math.min(100, $stress - 8))>>
<<set $anger = Math.max(0, Math.min(100, $anger - 4))>>
You count square breaths. The attic loosens a notch; boards settle, and the quiet thins to something you can stand inside without shaking.
<p class="dialogue">Fine. Breathe. I'll take what quiet you buy, even if it costs you.</p>
<p class="dialogue">Sometimes I imagined monks up here. Then I laughed at myself. Joke's on me—I needed them.</p>
<<timedprogressbar $timer>>
  <<goto "c01s01p05">>
<</timedprogressbar>>
[[Act: Raise your gaze|c01s01p06]]

:: c01s01p09
<<set $stress = Math.max(0, Math.min(100, $stress + 4))>>
You peer beyond his shoulder. The boards creak; cold ripples your arms. The black between rafters seems to lean closer as if to overhear.
<p class="dialogue">Don't try the dark for answers. It only teaches you to love the questions you can't stand.</p>
<p class="dialogue">There was a time I'd sleep on these boards. Now they keep me awake on purpose.</p>
<<timedprogressbar $timer>>
  <<goto "c01s01p10">>
<</timedprogressbar>>
[[Act: Count breaths|c01s01p08]]

:: c01s01p10
<<set $stress = Math.max(0, Math.min(100, $stress + 6))>>
Edges blur at the center as you inch closer. The floor flexes under a cautious foot; the room holds its breath with you.
<p class="dialogue">Careful. The center isn't where you think. It's where the ground decides you're done.</p>
<p class="dialogue">This is the part where people ruin it by trying to fix me with hands.</p>
<<timedprogressbar $timer>>
  <<goto "c01s01p06">>
<</timedprogressbar>>
[[Act: Step closer to the center|c01s01p11]]

:: c01s01p11
The floor snaps your balance. Leon flinches hard; panic punches the scene apart. The dark clamps shut like a trap sprung by your weight.
[[Act: Respawn|c01s01p12]]

:: c01s01p12
Breath returns in a shiver. Shadows reseat. The attic recovers your original stillness, as if rewinding to the first position.
<<timedprogressbar $timer>>
  <<goto "c01s01p01">>
<</timedprogressbar>>

:: c01s01p13
<<set $stress = Math.max(0, Math.min(100, $stress - 2))>>
Your gentleness steadies him; you ease your hand away like a prayer undone. The muttering softens without breaking.
<p class="dialogue">Okay. That was... fine. Don't make a habit of grace; it goes to my head.</p>
<p class="dialogue">Space is a gift I don't deserve. Keep giving it anyway if you're stubborn.</p>
<<timedprogressbar $timer>>
  <<goto "c01s01p05">>
<</timedprogressbar>>
[[Act: Step back|c01s01p06]]

:: c01s01p14
The contact spikes old anger. He jerks away; the room turns hostile as his frame recoils. The moment collapses to black.
[[Act: Respawn|c01s01p15]]

:: c01s01p15
He recoils, then settles. The attic rewrites the distance, returning you to a safer remove that funnels back to the beginning stance.
<<timedprogressbar $timer>>
  <<goto "c01s01p01">>
<</timedprogressbar>>

:: c01s01p16
Touch hangs on a knife-edge. If his stress or anger runs high, the gesture curdles; if low, patience buys another breath.
<p class="dialogue">Easy. Easy. My back isn't a switch you can flip. It remembers things I don't want.</p>
<p class="dialogue">If you keep your hand, keep your mercy with it. Otherwise leave me to the draft.</p>
<<if $anger > 4 || $stress > 10 || visited("c01s01p16") >= 2>>
  <<timedprogressbar $timer>>
    <<goto "c01s01p14">>
  <</timedprogressbar>>
<<else>>
  <<timedprogressbar $timer>>
    <<goto "c01s01p05">>
  <</timedprogressbar>>
<</if>>
[[Act: Withdraw your hand|c01s01p13]]

